    {
      "id": "cart-title",
      "name": "Title Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -380
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Handle Abandoned Cart\n\nHandler for one store event: a checkout was started (event 'checkout_created'). It tracks the cart in GoHighLevel and, if the customer has not ordered after the waiting time, sends ONE reminder. Shopify sends several events per checkout (the email arrives in a checkout update), so a checkout already tracked is skipped at once.\n\n**Called by:** the main workflow '[GHL Store Automation] | WF1 - Store Events & Win-Back' (its 'Run ... Handler' node, chosen by 'Route By Event Type'), which passes the normalised event together with the store settings. **Standalone-capable:** no.\n\n**Sections on this canvas:**\n1. Track The Cart And Remind\n\nGoHighLevel work is done by the GHL Adapter workflow (mock or live, chosen by 'ghl_adapter_id') and email by the Email Sender workflow (both called with Execute Workflow). Any failure is reported to the central error handler with THIS workflow's name and the failed node's name.",
        "width": 3540,
        "height": 340,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cart-sec",
      "name": "Section 1 Note - Track The Cart And Remind",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Track the cart and remind\n\nTriggered by: the main workflow's 'Run ... Handler' node, event 'checkout_created'.\n\nWhat it does, step by step:\n1. Stops at once if the checkout is already in the ghl_store_checkouts table (Shopify sends one event per change of the same checkout; only the first one with an email goes on). The first one is claimed at once in the table ('Claim Checkout Record', upper branch, runs before the slow GoHighLevel call), so an event that arrives a second later already stops here. Those later events take the lower path instead: Find Tracked Checkout → Refresh Stored Checkout Details saves their newest email, phone, names, cart and recovery link (an empty field never erases a stored one).\n2. Puts the contact in stage Cart Created (never backwards) and tags it 'cart-open'.\n3. Records the checkout in the ghl_store_checkouts table, with every customer and cart field.\n4. Waits (cart_wait_seconds: 1 hour in production, 2 minutes in the demo, so a real Shopify checkout can finish before the reminder).\n5. Looks the checkout up again, now with the newest details. If it was converted to an order, or a reminder was already sent, it stops.\n6. Otherwise sends the reminder from the stored details: always an email, plus an SMS when there is a phone number (the email is the channel every customer has and the one a demo can show).\n7. Records the reminder in the table and tags the contact 'cart-reminder-sent', sending GoHighLevel the newest phone and names too.",
        "width": 3540,
        "height": 1000,
        "color": 5
      }
    },
